# OpenClaw local dashboard (historical experiment)

Do not commit dashboard authentication tokens or URLs containing `#token=`.

Example SSH tunnel from your laptop to a private host:

```bash
ssh -N -L 18789:127.0.0.1:18789 <user>@<private-host>
```

Then open `http://127.0.0.1:18789/` and authenticate using the token or method configured **outside Git**.

The previous dashboard token appeared in Git history. Rotate it if that service can still be reached; editing this file does not remove historical exposure.
